    "name": "count-min-a-floor-leaves-a-window-it-can-only-see-part-of-unjudged",
    "why": "Owner decision L, and it is the asymmetry the whole window machinery turns on: a partial window makes both directions under-count, which is harmless for a cap and a false positive EVERY time for a floor, because the duties it cannot see are precisely the ones that would have met the number. The evaluable range here is the horizon itself, so the week reaching back to 26 July and the week reaching forward to 15 August are both partial, both left unjudged and both REPORTED — a silently dropped window is a guard that looks green. Only the middle week is measured, where p-ali is one short and p-zaid, who holds no duty at all, is two short. p-zaid is the second half of the case: a floor iterating duties rather than the roster would never see the person a floor exists to find.",
